                        ],
                        "form": "чисти́лищах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29d1a076-eaf1-3250-bb78-60f92a90af02",
                        "entry_id": "d88587e2-405e-3ef1-9dad-e4b4711cc33c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ. согласно католическому вероучению — место, где души умерших грешников очищаются от не искуплённых при жизни грехов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "45ecefb7-1512-39d1-9f38-4a2689cbc683",
                        "entry_id": "d88587e2-405e-3ef1-9dad-e4b4711cc33c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. временное место страданий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35e70114-fc6f-4933-aaae-e0e20386d023",
                                "sense_id": "45ecefb7-1512-39d1-9f38-4a2689cbc683",
                                "text": "Наступал конец второго учебного года, а с ним и конец учения в духовном училище, о чем все мы, выпускные, мечтали, как об освобождении из чистилища"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d97bdcfc-7e7e-4dfa-b00a-55672277c4e0",
                                "sense_id": "45ecefb7-1512-39d1-9f38-4a2689cbc683",
                                "text": "Я умерла заживо и уже терплю загробные муки. Это чистилище какое-то! ― терзалась Людмила Александровна в одиночестве своем, ломая холодный руки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf6a8979-bc9f-3465-ae2e-6d3177b8fc6c",
                        "entry_id": "d88587e2-405e-3ef1-9dad-e4b4711cc33c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. место, где что-либо чистят, вычищают"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "098375d7-a993-48cc-936e-acf05f0f06ee",
                                "sense_id": "cf6a8979-bc9f-3465-ae2e-6d3177b8fc6c",
                                "text": "Писания свои прилежно вычищай: Ведь из чистилища лишь идут в рай."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72fb4b4c-778e-4986-bd76-eb379430f6dc",
                                "sense_id": "cf6a8979-bc9f-3465-ae2e-6d3177b8fc6c",
                                "text": "Освободившись из карантинного чистилища, я поскакал в Царство Польское по прямой дороге, считая ее, как следовало думать, ближайшим путем к месту моего назначения."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8d60fb22-587e-4b61-bcc9-37cdf41325df",
                        "source_entry_id": "d88587e2-405e-3ef1-9dad-e4b4711cc33c",
                        "target_lang_word": "purgatory",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "purgatory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4006945c-b930-32d3-a6a5-6f2481de84ff",
                                        "entry_id": "41f8a1d8-2aed-3b77-bf1c-c05db54ea016",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Purgatory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                        "entry_id": "41f8a1d8-2aed-3b77-bf1c-c05db54ea016",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any situation where suffering is endured, particularly as part of a process of redemption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8d95700-eceb-46c9-8080-481fdce82be8",
                                                "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                                "text": "[…] many Gods breedeth heathens miseries, many countries trauailers humors, many wiues mens purgatories, and many friends trustes ruine:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11f3161d-c537-4b6c-98a4-d6b4c74a85cc",
                                                "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                                "text": "I laid my rank and fortune at the fair one’s feet, and would have married instantly; but that Oldworth opposed my precipitancy, and insisted upon a probation of six months absence—It has been a purgatory!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e31679a7-33d5-46fd-93c4-34b83e7b9ba7",
                                                "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                                "text": "It might be […] that Ruth had worked her way through the deep purgatory of repentance up to something like purity again; God only knew!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9139a66c-53ce-4912-ba08-a29bd013826c",
                                                "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                                "text": "Later came midsummer, with the stifling heat, when the dingy killing beds of Durham’s became a very purgatory; one time, in a single day, three men fell dead from sunstroke."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06df2f72-acc0-4b70-bfda-616c54a9c70f",
                                                "sense_id": "444d5fa9-f829-3b67-8bc5-43da1c994d07",
                                                "text": "[…] that would mean he would be irrecoverably Afrikaans and would have to spend years in the purgatory of an Afrikaans boarding-school, as all farm-children do, before he would be allowed to come back to the farm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "purgatory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa50d7bd-5ab0-38b4-9499-07233b24074c",
                                        "entry_id": "d720f3ed-8387-321a-9d86-958e6ed699c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tending to cleanse; expiatory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3f3db6-ea6e-4abe-9abb-dd8dbaede77d",
                                                "sense_id": "fa50d7bd-5ab0-38b4-9499-07233b24074c",
                                                "text": "Last of all, the prodigie of Siracusa was expiat by a purgatory sacrifice, by direction from the soothsaiers to what gods, supplications and sacrifice should be made."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cffd536b-ee80-4f04-8b47-1c90a58752e3",
                                                "sense_id": "fa50d7bd-5ab0-38b4-9499-07233b24074c",
                                                "text": "This purgatory interval is not unfavourable to a faithless representative, who may be as good a canvasser as he was a bad governor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
